<title>CANADA: Canada December, 1996 trade surpluses widen.</title>
<headline>Canada December, 1996 trade surpluses widen.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's merchandise trade surplus widened in December to C$2.37 billion from C$2.06 billion (revised from C$1.82 billion) in November, Statistics Canada said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The surplus for all of 1996 rose to C$34.13 billion from C$28.39 in 1995.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Dec 96  Nov 96   Dec 95</p>
<p>    Exports		22.32    22.57    21.75</p>
<p>    Imports		19.96    20.50    18.81</p>
<p>    Trade balance	+2.37    +2.06    +2.94</p>
</text>
